better at blending in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1501414-do-you-think-the-tall-man-from-phantasm-work-well-as-a-low-wisdom-mage?p=1501477#post1501477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it could be the Qlipoth of a Moros. Many of his capabilities could be Dread Powers, with being an Empty Shell explaining how he comes back and his minions emerging from the Abyssal Verge when certain conditions are met. He also gets 15 dots of Arcana, which can make him a very flexible antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if you want to start getting more specific like this, it's probably best to start thinking about if you want to make the Tall Man as an antagonist for mortals like in the films, or for mages, because that's going to very much impact what the best choices are when putting down mechanics. A Qlipoth feels like a better option for loosely adapting the Tall Man to a Mage game, than trying to directly replicate the character(s) as presented (not that this is bad, just what kind of creative choice is being made).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T10:37:10-08:00","id":1501544,"title":"","content":"I shou